## Stop merging on subject alone

The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe/) and
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) still prescribe subject matching.
Their review date is old, and the executable examples contradict that advice.
The accepted decision remains unchanged as historical evidence; this investigation recommends
a replacement decision rather than silently rewriting it.

Look up the tenant, locale, form version, and entry channel. Merge only when the failure mechanism
matches an existing issue. A matching subject is a search aid, not proof. If the tenant or mechanism
is unknown, keep the report separate pending investigation; do not default to merging.

<DedupeExplorer />

